-- Pinellas J gap-fill — 23 case_numbers with NO bid_decisions row at all.
-- Target: criterion J (Shapira deal thesis completeness), pinellas 388/411 (94.4%) -> aim 411/411.
--
-- CONTEXT / ROOT-CAUSE NOTE (read before touching this county again):
-- The existing 388 pinellas bid_decisions rows are NOT a reliable reference pattern to copy.
-- Live inspection this session found:
--   - 364 of 388 rows (pipeline_version='shapira_v14_inferred', inserted in a single
--     2026-06-24T08:23:49-50 burst, ~1 second) share a CONSTANT ml_score=0.7200 and constant
--     factors.distress_location=0.65/distress_property=0.60/distress_owner=0.55 across every
--     row regardless of the underlying property. This is the exact "ghost success" signature
--     (constant score, single-timestamp bulk insert) that has been identified and purged
--     elsewhere in this campaign (glades, sumter, walton — see
--     migrations/20260721_gold_standard_shard9_hillsborough_glades_suwannee_j_ghost_success_purge.sql
--     and migrations/20260728_architect_triage_15799_sumter_j_real_comps.sql). Its arv_source
--     is 'mca_assessed_value' (a formula off multi_county_auctions fields only, no real comps).
--   - The remaining 24 rows (pipeline_version='shard4_run3713_j_gen_v1',
--     arv_source='shapira_formula_pinellas_shard4_run3713') are also formula-derived, not
--     comps-based.
-- Per the task scope given for this session, the existing 388 rows are OUT OF SCOPE and are
-- NOT touched, modified, or re-litigated here. This note is left so a future session does not
-- mistake the existing 94.4% baseline for a verified-real baseline — most of it is not, and
-- the true county completeness (by the "real per-property comps" bar this migration meets)
-- is lower than the naive percentage suggests. Flagging this explicitly per HONESTY PROTOCOL /
-- NEVER-LIE rather than silently building on top of a known-fabricated pattern.
--
-- DIAGNOSIS OF THE 23-ROW GAP (verified live 2026-08-01): all 23 case_numbers have a
-- multi_county_auctions row with a real parcel_id and assessed_value but NO bid_decisions row
-- at all (fully missing, not partially incomplete).
--
-- PARCEL-ID FORMAT DISCOVERY (why the fleet-standard fl_parcels join initially returned zero
-- matches for this county): multi_county_auctions.parcel_id for pinellas is the 18-digit
-- concatenated PIN (e.g. "163029287820000071"). public.fl_parcels stores pinellas under
-- co_no=62 (VERIFIED live by phy_city cross-check: co_no=62 rows are Clearwater/Largo/St
-- Petersburg/Palm Harbor/Seminole/Pinellas Park, i.e. genuinely Pinellas County -- co_no=52,
-- which would be the naive FL-DOR-standard guess for Pinellas, is actually mislabeled Marion
-- County data (Ocala/Dunnellon/Belleview) in this table -- co_no in this table does NOT
-- follow standard FL DOR numbering for at least these two values) using the county's own STRAP
-- format "SS TT RR SUBDIV BLOCK LOT" (space-separated, e.g. "16 30 29 28782 000 0071"). The
-- leading section/township/range triplet is NOT stored in a fixed digit order between the two
-- systems (verified by cases where a naive positional decode produced a permutation of the
-- correct triplet, e.g. mca encodes "24 30 15" where fl_parcels stores "15 30 24" for the same
-- physical parcel). The trailing 12 digits (5-digit subdivision + 3-digit block + 4-digit lot)
-- ARE stable and unique across co_no=62, and every one of the 23 targets matches exactly one
-- fl_parcels row on that suffix, independently confirmed by exact real-world street address
-- equality (phy_addr1) for all 23. This suffix-match is the join key used below.
--
-- METHODOLOGY (same convention as public.gen_valuations_comps_batch() and the sumter/glades J
-- fixes: real fl_parcels.sale_prc1 comps, same zip + dor_uc, living-area tolerance, tiered):
--   Tier 1: same phy_zipcd + dor_uc, living-area (tot_lvg_ar) within 0.7x-1.3x, sold >=2022.
--   Tier 2 (fallback): same phy_zipcd + dor_uc, living-area within 0.5x-2.0x, sold >=2018.
-- Live dry-run this session: ALL 23 targets clear Tier 1 with n_comps ranging 14-469 (no row
-- needed tier 2, no row fell through to "no data"). ARV = GREATEST(real assessed_value from
-- multi_county_auctions, real fl_parcels av_sd, tier-1 comp median). cma_distressed/cma_resale
-- = real tier-1 p25/p75 (VERIFIED, not a flat multiplier of ARV). ml_score and the three
-- distress_* factors are a documented, disclosed formula (opening_bid/assessed_value
-- distress-gap + comp-pool-size confidence, same formula shape as
-- migrations/20260725_gold_standard_shard12_glades_j_countywide_comps_run6288.sql) -- these
-- are INFERRED, not output of a trained model; no fleet script actually invokes a live
-- Shapira V14 model at row-insert time, this is the same disclosed-methodology convention used
-- by every other fleet J-fix referenced above.
--
-- HONESTY_TAG: VERIFIED for arv/cma_distressed/cma_resale (real fl_parcels.sale_prc1
-- percentiles, re-queried live immediately before writing this file) and for the
-- parcel/address join (independently confirmed by exact street-address match for all 23).
-- INFERRED for ml_score/distress_owner/distress_location/distress_property (documented
-- formula below, not a trained-model score).
--
-- Adversarial refuter validation SQL (run AFTER applying):
--   SELECT COUNT(*) AS total, COUNT(DISTINCT ml_score) AS distinct_ml,
--     COUNT(DISTINCT arv) AS distinct_arv,
--     COUNT(DISTINCT (factors->'cma_distressed'->>'value')) AS distinct_cma_d,
--     COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE pipeline_version IS NULL) AS null_pv,
--     COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE (factors->>'distress_owner')::numeric = ml_score) AS dup_do
--   FROM bid_decisions WHERE county_slug='pinellas'
--     AND pipeline_version='pinellas_j_23row_backfill_v1';
--   Expected: total=23, distinct_ml=23 (or very close), distinct_arv=23, distinct_cma_d=23,
--   null_pv=0, dup_do=0.

SET statement_timeout = 0;

-- PERFORMANCE NOTE: an earlier draft of this migration ran the tier-1/tier-2 comps lookup as a
-- correlated subquery per target row directly inside the INSERT (matching the glades/sumter
-- migrations' style). Live execution against the Supabase Management API timed out (>120s,
-- twice) because that shape re-scans a slice of fl_parcels once per row per tier inside a single
-- statement. The comps values themselves were independently computed with the exact same
-- SQL logic (verified by a separate, successful SELECT-only run against the live DB
-- immediately before writing this file — see the "VALUES" literals below, each one traceable
-- to a real fl_parcels percentile_cont() query result, not hand-picked). This version inlines
-- those already-computed real values as a literal VALUES list so the live INSERT is a simple,
-- fast multi-row insert. No computation changed; only how the result got expressed in SQL.

